WEBVTT

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.510
"Warning"

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.340
Hurry!

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.350
It won't shut!

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.410
Well, will it work?

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.830
Hurry up!

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.460
Damn it!

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.050
Hey, what the hell is that?

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.590
What's going on?! I need that data now!

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.430
--Hurry up!
--I've never seen
the Extinction Belt this low.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.890
--I need a visual on monitor 2!
--I've never seen
the Extinction Belt this low.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:01.680
Others are spawning in abnormal numbers!
There's no sign it's abating!

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.860
Yuito.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.980
What's your ETA?

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.360
Thirty minutes.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.860
I see.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:17.070
How's it look out there?

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.660
Pretty bad.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.330
The intermittent shaking
has yet to subside.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.660
It's causing the defense system
to keep glitching.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:29.250
Plus, the Extinction Belt is descending
to an extremely low elevation.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:34.920
The Kunad Gate's increased activity
must be causing a gravitational anomaly.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.300
If the Belt continues to descend...

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.050
How's Yuito?

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.640
He's still unconscious.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:46.430
And he seems to be in pain at times.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:48.940
I'll have a hospital bed ready.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:54.570
But under the current circumstances,
I don't know how much they can do for him.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:56.700
Okay, thanks.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:32.870
"The Sumeragi Mausoleum"

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.790
"The Sumeragi Mausoleum"

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.790
Yuito, hang in there.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.880
Hanabi, I know you're worried,

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:46.100
but they told us teleporting Yuito
would be risky in his condition.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.430
I know. Sorry, Luka.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:50.520
No worries.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.770
Is he gonna be okay?
He hasn't even opened his eyes.

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.360
Don't say that!

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.690
He's not done yet.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:05.820
You should've heard the self-conceited
tone he took towards me.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:12.460
He won't go down easy, not until he shows
me what he considers the right path.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:16.840
That sounds a lot like you, Chief.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:21.800
Your authority has been temporarily
restored due to the state of emergency.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:27.930
That means you can take command
of the OSF as soon as we reach Suoh.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:32.600
So they want to use and abuse me
before they throw me out.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.310
What an impressive political decision.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.980
The defense system's down!
And it won't be back up anytime soon!

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:43.450
Arahabaki is a rock-solid system.
It'll recover in no time!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:46.070
The blast doors at some
shelters won't shut.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:50.490
The OSF is holding the Others at bay,
but they won't last long!

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.700
We're seriously short on personnel!

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.460
Our lines are collapsing,
and we can't coordinate our defense.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.500
Abandon the defense system positions
that aren't functioning.

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:04.760
Chief Sumeragi!

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:10.010
Soldiers at the inoperable anti-Other flak
cannons should shift to shelter defense.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.810
And have all splinter forces
immediately fall back to HQ.

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:15.890
We'll reform our lines.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.860
Seiran and Togetsu are facing
the same situation.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.820
We can't call for backup.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.280
The future of New Himuka
is in our own hands!

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:25.700
Yes, sir!

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.410
Well done, handling things so far.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.620
I'm grateful.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.500
Th-Thank you, sir!

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.420
Fire, fire!

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:54.310
Are you all right?

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:57.940
We cleared out the area around
the eastern district's shelter.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.770
We were in time here, too!

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:03.940
Understood. When the situation stabilizes,
head to another shelter.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:15.950
Where am I?

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.460
The hospital in Suoh?

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.750
It happened to me again?

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:27.170
Everyone okay?

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.380
Yuito. You finally came to.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:30.930
What a relief.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.390
Yeah, um...

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:36.890
I remember there was an Others
alert in Suoh and then...

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:40.190
Their numbers have
significantly dwindled now.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:42.810
And their spawn rate has stabilized.

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:46.940
But it's still not safe for civilians
to leave the shelters.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:48.820
I see.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:51.870
The defense system has yet to recover,

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:55.490
and we've no idea if Others
might overrun the city again.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:57.620
We're standing by at HQ.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:00.920
And in the meantime,
we're trying to regroup.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:04.710
I'll head for the Sumeragi Mausoleum
as soon as I can.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.220
Yuito, are you sure you're all right?

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:12.640
No need to worry about me.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.970
That long nap did wonders.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:18.810
But now we have to find Yakumo,
or should I say Karen,

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:20.690
and unravel the last entanglement.

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:25.270
It must be done before we reach
the point of no return.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:26.860
Understood.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:32.160
But since you just came to,
let's wait until we're sure you're better.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.700
Okay, got it.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.580
The Sumeragi Mausoleum.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:48.090
Yuito... You really think he's okay?

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:52.050
If he says he is,
there's not much we can do.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:57.350
You're right. All we can do
is worry about ourselves.

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:03.060
If my brother is at the mausoleum,
we can ask him to hear us out.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.810
But if he won't listen...

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:08.530
It might turn into a fight.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:11.820
Yes.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.240
We must be ready for anything.

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:21.710
I know this world is full
of ugliness and injustice.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:26.920
But even after all that's gone wrong,
I'd never want to bring it to an end.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:31.920
No matter what happens,
I will <i>never </i>give up on the world.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.140
What's so funny?

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.810
Let's see here.

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:41.100
What's that?

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:43.060
I'm looking at this gyoza joint.

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:45.100
--Huh?
--I've been meaning to try it.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.440
Gyoza?!

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:50.030
Yeah, but it attracts a young crowd.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:51.900
I'd feel out of place.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:55.530
In that case, how about I join you?

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.700
I'm not that young, but...

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:59.200
I'll go, too.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:02.000
You can count me in, as well!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:07.250
I'm trying to be serious,
but you guys just screw around!

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:11.050
That's because the world will be fine
as long as you're around.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:15.050
We need people like you
thinking about the future.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:21.770
I kind of like gyoza, too.

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.980
What are you thinking about?

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.190
Tsugumi.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.900
It's just...

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:41.120
I was wondering if you were gonna go, too.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.490
Yes.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:45.960
There are so many people
I care about here.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.080
I couldn't bear it if they died.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.000
You feel the same, don't you?

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:54.050
I do, but...

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:56.260
You won't reconsider?

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.550
What?

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:05.980
I don't know if I'd be able to protect you
if we have to fight Karen.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:09.650
I want you to live a long life.

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:14.150
I never wanted to live my life
under your protection.

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:16.320
That goes for the future, too.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:20.070
You're right.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:23.580
I mean, who am I to say that to you?

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.830
It's all right.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:33.630
I'm sure we'll all live another day
to laugh at your wisecracks.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.460
You will live, too.

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:37.550
That was mean, Tsugumi.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:39.720
I'm always 100% serious.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.430
There you go again.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.810
No, no, it's true!

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.570
You haven't changed a bit, Sis.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:59.200
What do you mean?

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.490
Where should I begin?

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:04.830
How about not lounging around
snacking in other people's rooms?

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.660
Don't mind me. I'm good.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:10.960
I've got an early day tomorrow.
I better get to bed.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:13.500
Okay, you do you?

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.210
Sis!

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:19.010
It's time for you to go!

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:21.010
Jeez.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:22.970
You're no fun.

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:26.680
Your big sis doesn't remember
raising you like that.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:29.430
And I don't remember you raising me.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.560
I saw that one coming.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:37.650
Sis, about tomorrow...

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:41.820
We got this. The Others
won't know what hit 'em.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:48.540
But I'd be careful who I was
friendly with if I were you.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.620
Yuito, don't tell me...

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:35.330
Kasane.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:37.290
I'm glad I came to check on you.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:38.960
I thought you might not be ready.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:40.010
I'm fine.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.010
But what about your psionics?

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:43.550
No, listen!

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:49.140
Nagi, Naomi, Commander Seto...

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.640
I still can't believe they're gone.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:59.440
And I don't think I'll ever get over it,
no matter how much time passes.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:06.110
This world is built on those who lost
their lives and the resulting sorrow.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:11.700
Seeking to rewind time with psionics
or attain even greater psionic power

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:17.000
has shattered the lives
of countless people.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.710
This has to end.

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:25.260
We let this be a world where
everything is done just for power.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:31.220
We were supposed to be
the masters of psionic power,

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:35.190
but it ended up mastering us
before we knew it.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.900
That's my point.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:42.360
I seek a world where we can live without
everything depending on such power.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:45.650
For that to happen,
the Kunad Gate must be eliminated.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.030
You give me hope.

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:53.410
I honestly thought you were next
to useless when I first met you.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.000
Yeah, I picked up on that.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:00.090
But you're different now.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:04.710
I think you really are capable
of changing the world.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.590
Thanks for saying that.

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:10.140
Don't mention it. Now I can go outside.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.470
What do you mean "outside"?

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.020
Yuito, Kasane. You there?

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.230
--Yeah.
--Yes.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:19.560
It's time. We move out in 15 minutes.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:20.810
Got it.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:22.360
We'll be right there.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:24.780
Let's go.

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:26.440
Together.

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:27.650
Okay.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.370
Be careful.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:42.290
Even I can't get data on what's inside
the Sumeragi Mausoleum.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.920
So then we're going in blind.

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:00.770
What is this?

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.910
What the hell is this?

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:15.660
This looks like... OSF HQ?!

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.200
How'd we end up here?

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:21.920
Maybe someone used the transport
power on us, or it's a trap!

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:26.340
All right, all right. Let's calm down
and assess the situation.

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:28.800
Something's clearly not right here.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:32.510
My guess is it has to do
with my brother's power.

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:40.940
An Others alert has been issued!
Others are descending in large numbers.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.730
Prepare to engage.

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:58.500
The Others spawn rate is increasing again.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:19.560
It's my brother!

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:20.520
Karen?!

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:21.810
Luka, wait!

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:25.020
That's most likely not really Karen!

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:27.150
All we can do is follow!

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:37.280
This is the same place my sister was.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:06.020
Sis.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:10.440
Kasane, look out!

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:19.240
We'll be trapped like rats.
Let's get out of here!

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:20.120
Kasane!

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:21.410
I know!

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:29.420
Looks like we're not gonna
get out of this so easy.

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:42.680
Gemma! Above you!

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:01.790
What is this place?

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:13.130
Nagi.

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:26.810
This is that time we...!

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:36.900
What is this?

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:41.830
We're experiencing the pain and agony...

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:43.870
...my brother suffered.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:19:00.220
We can all be together forever.

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:17.110
I can't take it!

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:23.280
It's no use. It's swallowing me up.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:29.660
We can all be together forever.

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:45.180
We can all be together forever.

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:50.770
Together forever.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:27.060
So I've failed once again.

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:40.860
Thank you, Kasane.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.990
Sis!

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:46.660
Sis!

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:53.000
Thank you, Kasane.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:56.000
Live the life that

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.250
I couldn't have.

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:03.380
Sis!

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:12.980
What was that?

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.150
Is everyone okay?

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:19.730
We have to get out of here.

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:21.230
Let's go.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:32.410
Is that...?

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:36.370
I'm not done yet.

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:39.040
Not yet. Bring it on.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:09.070
Yakumo...

00:22:09.070 --> 00:22:10.990
...Sumeragi?

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:41.820
<i>I've been a prisoner</i>
<i>of my own longing</i>

00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:51.450
<i>The shimmering heat signals me to halt</i>

00:22:51.450 --> 00:22:53.580
<i>There's a stranger in me</i>

00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:56.080
<i>I'll fly high so I won't be scared</i>

00:22:56.080 --> 00:23:01.330
<i>By this new self I've never seen</i>

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:03.130
<i>I'm spreading my wings</i>

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:05.460
<i>Bird in florid flight</i>

00:23:05.460 --> 00:23:10.180
<i>Lift your eyes to the scarlet sky</i>

00:23:10.180 --> 00:23:15.390
<i>Overtaken by the mighty wind</i>

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:20.560
<i>The view unfolds upon a world</i>
<i>that begins turning</i>

00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:25.030
<i>Amid the intermingling light</i>

00:23:25.030 --> 00:23:30.910
<i>I keep searching for tomorrow</i>

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:32.530
<i>Tomorrow's in your hands</i>

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:35.740
<i>Don't tell me now you're afraid</i>

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:37.370
<i>There's no time to waste</i>

00:23:37.370 --> 00:23:40.330
<i>Keep going forward</i>

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:44.670
<i>There's nothing to be afraid of</i>

00:23:44.670 --> 00:23:46.340
<i>Now, let's go</i>

00:23:46.340 --> 00:23:51.800
<i>Into a brand-new day</i>

00:24:09.070 --> 00:24:11.910
"Slumbering Desire"
